We compute the ratio \( \frac{g(G)^3}{f(G)^4} \) for \( K_n \): \[
\frac{\left( \binom{n}{4} \right)^3}{\left( \binom{n}{3} \right)^4} = \frac{\left( \frac{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}{24} \right)^3}{\left( \frac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{6} \right)^4}
\]

Simplifying this expression: \[
\frac{\left( \frac{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}{24} \right)^3}{\left( \frac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{6} \right)^4} = \frac{(n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3))^3 / 24^3}{(n(n-1)(n-2))^4 / 6^4} = \frac{(n-3)^3 \cdot 6^4}{n(n-1)(n-2) \cdot 24^3}
\]

Further simplifying the constants: \[
\frac{6^4}{24^3} = \frac{1296}{13824} = \frac{3}{32}
\]

Thus, the ratio simplifies to: \[
\frac{3}{32} \cdot \frac{(n-3)^3}{n(n-1)(n-2)}
\]

Therefore, the least constant \( c \) such that \( g(G)^3 \leq c \cdot f(G)^4 \) for every graph \( G \) is: \[
\boxed{\dfrac{3}{32}}
\]
